{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":258413,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3e53b8de-aff0-4e6a-bd0e-929ff5709662","total_cost_usd":1.031682,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":44687,"cache_read_input_tokens":20278,"output_tokens":21771,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":44687,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":21771,"cache_read_input_tokens":20278,"cache_creation_input_tokens":44687,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":44687},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":30308,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.030388000000000002,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":21771,"cacheReadInputTokens":20278,"cacheCreationInputTokens":44687,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.001294,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"debris-designer\",\n  \"size_classes\": {\n    \"small\": {\n      \"slots_crushed\": 1,\n      \"slots_uncrushed\": 2,\n      \"hand_tetherable\": true\n    },\n    \"medium\": {\n      \"slots_crushed\": 2,\n      \"slots_uncrushed\": 4,\n      \"hand_tetherable\": true\n    },\n    \"oversized\": {\n      \"slots_crushed\": 6,\n      \"slots_uncrushed\": 12,\n      \"hand_tetherable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  \"debris\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"bent_truss_section\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Bent Truss Section\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 430,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"A folded aluminium lattice off a broken solar boom — the bread-and-butter haul of the low sky, cheap per kilo but it crushes flat and never argues on the way down.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"crumpled_foil_blanket\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Crumpled Foil Blanket\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 45,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 16,\n      \"notes\": \"A whole satellite's worth of shredded multi-layer insulation balled up and tumbling — the lightest thing in the sky by a factor of five, which makes it the piece a beginner learns the tether on.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"burnt_panel_offcut\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Burnt Panel Offcut\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 85,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 13,\n      \"notes\": \"A scorched honeycomb face sheet torn off a bus panel, already half-cooked by its own decaying orbit and worth taking only because it costs almost nothing to carry.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"spent_bolt_cluster\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Spent Bolt Cluster\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 130,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 15,\n      \"notes\": \"A knot of frangible separation bolts still welded to their collar — dense lumps of good steel that Armstrong will always take off your hands.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_antenna_whip\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Antenna Whip\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 35,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 5,\n      \"notes\": \"A hairline-split monopole that glints on a slow cycle across the whole band — the cheapest possible lesson in what fragile costs you, since it weighs nothing and still can't be crushed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scorched_hull_plate\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Scorched Hull Plate\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 700,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 7,\n      \"notes\": \"A curved slab of pressure-vessel skin with its ring frames still attached, the heaviest thing down here that a hand magnet will hold — three and a half times the average piece, and the first load that makes the jetpack feel like it's pushing a train.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"dented_pressure_bottle\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Dented Pressure Bottle\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 380,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A spent cold-gas tank, vented and safe, packing more mass into one crushed slot than anything else in the band — the best mass-to-slot bargain the low sky offers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"shattered_lens_cowl\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Shattered Lens Cowl\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 70,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"The glass sunshade off a cheap earth-imager, spidered but intact, orbiting well clear of the common clumps so reaching it is a deliberate crossing rather than a drift.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"collapsed_launch_shroud\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Collapsed Launch Shroud\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1100,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"Half a payload fairing, folded like a dropped umbrella — mostly enclosed air, so it is bulk rather than tonnage, and crane-cable only regardless. It sits in the sky all semester as a visible advertisement for an upgrade the shipping slice does not sell.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"reaction_wheel_housing\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Reaction Wheel Housing\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 870,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A cast steel gimbal block with the flywheel still seized inside — the workhorse of the low band, solid enough to shrug off a mediocre landing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"severed_solar_wing_spar\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Severed Solar Wing Spar\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 760,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"The load-bearing backbone of an array with the cells sheared away, long enough that it swings wide on every turn and teaches the player to stop before slewing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_solar_array\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Solar Array\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 390,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 6,\n      \"notes\": \"A wing panel of intact gallium cells behind fractured cover glass — the signature fragile piece of the slice, four uncrushed slots forever and double damage from every mistake.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"battery_pack_module\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Battery Pack Module\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1150,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 8,\n      \"notes\": \"A brick of lithium cells in a machined frame — the heaviest hand-tetherable piece in the shipping slice, and the one that decides whether a two-tether string is a good idea.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"thruster_nozzle_bell\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Thruster Nozzle Bell\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 340,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 11,\n      \"notes\": \"A niobium bell off an attitude thruster, dense and compact, the piece that makes a one-slot capture feel worth the crossing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"star_tracker_head\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Star Tracker Head\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 155,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 4,\n      \"notes\": \"A baffled optical head the size of a beer keg, light for the band and precious and utterly uncrushable — the cheapest way to learn that fragile is about bulk and risk, not weight.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tangled_harness_bundle\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Tangled Harness Bundle\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 210,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 12,\n      \"notes\": \"A snarl of copper loom torn out of a bus, floppy on the cable and forgiving of every rough latch — the low band's filler, and its safety net on a thin run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"parabolic_dish_section\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Parabolic Dish Section\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 420,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"A quarter-segment of a mesh reflector on its own faster orbit, catching the light on a slow cycle — a real ship manoeuvre to reach and a patient closing rate to latch.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"derelict_upper_stage_tank\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Derelict Upper Stage Tank\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 2000,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A drained kick-stage tank the length of the rocket itself — thin-walled and hollow, so it is twelve uncrushed slots of nothing much, and crane-cable only. The piece the player circles once, measures with their eyes, and files away for later.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"comsat_bus_frame\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Comsat Bus Frame\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1950,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"The machined spine of a dead communications satellite, dense with fittings — the common piece of the top band and heavier on its own than most complete low-band hauls.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"hardened_avionics_core\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Hardened Avionics Core\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1600,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 8,\n      \"notes\": \"A radiation-shielded flight computer in a lead-lined box, built to survive anything the sky could do to it — which is exactly why it survives the ride down too.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cryo_propellant_sphere\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cryo Propellant Sphere\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 2200,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 8,\n      \"notes\": \"A thick-walled titanium sphere off a station-keeping system, the single heaviest thing a hand magnet will hold at any tier — one of these turns a routine reentry into a three-pass problem.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"momentum_gyro_cluster\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Momentum Gyro Cluster\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1150,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"Three control-moment gyros still bolted to their pedestal, absurdly dense for one crushed slot — the piece that proves mass, not volume, is what fills the top band's holds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"sensor_boom_mast\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Sensor Boom Mast\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 700,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 6,\n      \"notes\": \"A telescoping magnetometer boom, collapsed and locked — awkward to latch square, but it crushes into a single slot and asks nothing else of the flight home.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"gallium_solar_panel\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Gallium Solar Panel\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 920,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 6,\n      \"notes\": \"A full triple-junction wing off a high-orbit bird, worth several solid pieces of its own size class and worth nothing at all if the touchdown runs past five metres a second.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"optical_telescope_barrel\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Optical Telescope Barrel\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1300,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 5,\n      \"notes\": \"A mirrored assembly in a carbon tube, heavy and fragile at once — four uncrushed slots, double heat damage, and the best payday in the catalog short of the satellite itself.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"xenon_ion_grid\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Xenon Ion Grid\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 540,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A stack of etched molybdenum accelerator grids in their mounting cage, spawning far off the clumps at real relative velocity — the purest latch-jerk test in the game.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"high_gain_dish_assembly\",\n      \"display_name\": \"High-Gain Dish Assembly\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 3200,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A full reflector with its feed tower and gimbal still attached — crane-cable only, and the rehearsal piece for the satellite: same technique, same order of mass, forgiving cargo.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"armstrongs_satellite\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Armstrong's Satellite\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 3600,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 1,\n      \"notes\": \"The one he lost the day of the cascade, hanging above the top band — the heaviest object in the game, fragile and oversized, uncrushable at any tier, roughly doubling a fully upgraded ship on its own, and the win condition only if it comes down gently.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"band_summary\": [\n    {\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"piece_count\": 9,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.1,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 330.6\n    },\n    {\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"piece_count\": 9,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.2,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 699.4\n    },\n    {\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"piece_count\": 10,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.25,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 1716\n    }\n  ],\n  \"revision_notes\": [\n    \"Finding 1 accepted, one field moved: armstrongs_satellite goes 4,200 to 3,600 kg. The Balancer is right that 4,200 against 850 is 4.9x, but the ship the doubling is measured against is not the 850 kg starting ship — a base ship cannot reach the top of the sky at all, and GDD 2.3.7 stages the capstone explicitly 'at full upgrades'. dry_mass_kg 850 is pinned by the starting-storage case and should stay pinned; what had to move is the satellite, and 3,600 is twice the fully upgraded ship mass I am naming below.\",\n    \"Finding 1, the number the Balancer needs so it does not have to re-derive it: the upgrade ladder has to land a maxed ship near 1,800 kg dry, which is 2.1x the base 850. That is storage 6 to 12 slots (racking and a tier-3 compactor are the bulk of it), the hull upgrade, a thicker shield plate, and the crane magnet with its winch drum — an unbolted car-crusher magnet welded to the rocket is not a light part, and the capstone cannot be flown without it. If the upgrade table lands materially below 1,800, route it back and I will move the satellite again: it is the one piece in the catalog whose mass is a pure function of ship mass rather than of what it plausibly is.\",\n    \"Finding 1, why 2x and not 1x. 'Roughly doubles the ship's mass on its own' could be read as the 2.3.5 convention (cargo equals dry, total goes to 2x), which would put the satellite at 1,800 kg. I rejected that reading: at 1,800 the capstone descent is exactly as heavy as a beginner's first full hold, and GDD 2.3.7 promises 'the fattest, hottest, worst-handling descent the player will ever fly'. At 3,600 on an 1,800 kg ship the capstone flies at 3x dry mass, half again the beta of any other loaded return in the game, which is the only reading that makes the win condition the hardest flight rather than a repeat of the first one.\",\n    \"Finding 1, the piece I deliberately did not touch: high_gain_dish_assembly stays at 3,200. It is the rehearsal piece — same tool, same order of mass, forgiving cargo — and the satellite at 3,600 is still the heaviest object in the game, which is all GDD 2.3.7 requires. Pulling the dish down to widen the gap would re-author a piece no finding named.\",\n    \"Finding 2, measurement accepted, fix declined, and no mass changed. Recomputed against the 1,800 kg ship that can actually reach the high band, cryo_propellant_sphere is 1.22x the ship and comsat_bus_frame is 1.08x, not 2.6x. The 2.6x figure compares top-band junk to a starting ship that has neither the tank nor the thruster to get there, so it measures a flight nobody can fly.\",\n    \"Finding 2, the 6,600 kg figure is a hold the player has to construct on purpose. Six slots of nothing but cryo spheres is 6,600 kg, but the spawn-weighted high-band cargo runs 669.0 kg per crushed slot, so a representative six-slot high-band hold is 4,014 kg. Sweep the constructed worst case by all means — just do not price against it as the median.\",\n    \"Finding 2, the real risk restated with arithmetic, because it is worth more to the crew than a rescale would be. A maxed 12-slot hold of spawn-weighted high-band junk is 8,028 kg on an 1,800 kg ship: 9,828 kg total, which against the Researcher's shield Cd 1.5 and 3.1 m2 gives beta 2,113 kg/m2. On the Researcher's own drag ladder that is roughly 2 m/s2 at a 20 km periapsis, about 117 m/s a pass, so ten passes to shed 1,150 m/s — well outside the 2-4 pass corridor. The lever is not catalog mass. It is shield reference area and Cd at upgraded tiers (the Researcher holds 3.1 m2 fixed across every tier, which cannot be right for a plate you pay to upgrade), or band-gated ablation as GDD 4.5 risk 2 already proposes. Compressing high-band mass to fix it would delete the only band-to-band difficulty gradient the game has, since the Researcher has established that heat gives just 1.31x.\",\n    \"Bookkeeping correction to my own previous pass, so nobody inherits a mislabelled number: '214.5 kg per spawn-weighted cargo slot' was wrong on the label, not on the value. 214.5 kg is the spawn-weighted mean mass of a suborbital hand-tetherable piece. The per-slot figures are 164.0 kg fully crushed and 124.9 kg under a strict tier-1 compactor, which are what produce the 984 kg and 749 kg six-slot holds the Balancer used, so dry_mass_kg 850 is unaffected and remains correctly derived.\",\n    \"Nothing else changed. One field moved in the entire catalog — armstrongs_satellite.mass_kg — and the high band's mean_mass_kg follows it from 1,776 to 1,716. Every id, band, size_class, fragile flag, spawn_weight, note and every other mass is byte-identical to the previous catalog, and both fragile fractions and the other two band means are unchanged because nothing they depend on moved.\"\n  ],\n  \"design_notes\": [\n    \"Mass carries the difficulty curve because the Researcher says heat cannot, and the rescale of one oversized piece left that curve untouched. Hand-tetherable mean mass is 234.4 kg suborbital, 536.9 kg low, 1,295.0 kg high — steps of 2.29x and 2.41x, 5.5x end to end. Spawn-weighted, which is what the player actually meets, it is 214.5 / 559.0 / 1,426.4 kg — steps of 2.61x and 2.55x, 6.65x end to end. Per crushed cargo slot, spawn-weighted with fragile pieces charged their uncrushable cost, the bands run 164.0 / 291.1 / 669.0 kg.\",\n    \"The full-hold doubling in GDD 2.3.5 is true at the case the GDD specifies and nowhere else, and that is a property of the design rather than a defect in the catalog. A beginner with six slots and a tier-1 compactor comes home with 749 kg on an 850 kg ship; crushed optimally the same hold is 984 kg. Both bracket the ship. No single dry_mass_kg can also make it true in the high band, because a band that is only 31% hotter has to be several times heavier or it is not harder at all.\",\n    \"Fragile fraction is spawn-weighted and lands at exactly 0.10 / 0.20 / 0.25. The counts run the other way on purpose: suborbital has 2 fragile types out of 9 but they carry weights 5 and 3 against 80, so the player meets one about one time in ten, while the high band's 4 types out of 10 carry 6+5+2+1 against 56 for a true 0.25.\",\n    \"Every size class and the fragile flag appear inside the shipping slice. Suborbital and low each carry small, medium, fragile-small and fragile-medium, so a player who never buys past the hand magnet still meets the whole property space, and the two crane-only pieces below the high band exist to be looked at and not taken.\",\n    \"Medium is distributed 2 / 5 / 5 across the bands rather than piled into the top, so 'higher bands skew toward medium' stays true as a proportion — 22% / 56% / 50% of types — without turning the low band into a small-only tutorial.\",\n    \"No piece is strictly best, and the greed decision is between axes rather than along one. The dense smalls (dented pressure bottle at 380 kg in one crushed slot, momentum gyro cluster at 1,150) buy mass efficiency per slot at the cost of a heavier ride home; the light bulky ones (foil blanket, harness bundle) are nearly free to tow and nearly worthless per trip; fragile pieces pay a premium the Balancer sets but forfeit crushing forever and double every damage source.\",\n    \"The suborbital band teaches the tow mechanic by itself: 45 kg to 700 kg is a 15.6x spread inside the first band the player ever flies, so the beat in GDD 2.3.4 where the jetpack starts feeling like it is pushing a train has a piece to land on before the low band opens. The heaviest hand-tetherable piece per band — 700 / 1,150 / 2,200 kg — is the specific case the Playtester should sweep hold force and shear against at each magnet tier.\",\n    \"The oversized class is a statement about which tool takes a piece and how much hold it eats, never about mass, and the numbers say so: a folded fairing half at 1,100 kg, a drained kick stage at 2,000 and a dish assembly at 3,200 each cost six crushed slots or twelve uncrushed — more hold than a starting ship has — while weighing one to three times what a hand magnet will hold. That separation is what lets Armstrong's satellite be the heaviest object in the game and roughly double the ship at the same time.\",\n    \"Armstrong's satellite is authored into the high band at 3,600 kg because the GDD places it above the top band and there is no fourth band name to use. It is fragile and oversized with spawn weight 1, contributing 0.018 of the band's weight, so it does not distort the fragile gradient. Treat its band field as bookkeeping placement, not a spawn location: it is a fixed object, not a member of the loot table.\",\n    \"Suit mass remains the one number this catalog leans on and does not own. At a 90 kg suit the 700 kg hull plate leaves 11% of clean EVA acceleration and a two-piece string 7%, which is a wall rather than a train; at a realistic MMU-class 250 kg it is 26% and 15%, which is the handling GDD 2.3.4 describes. That is a config parameter, and it is still flagged rather than fixed.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":174510,"ttft_stream_ms":1564,"time_to_request_ms":254,"type":"result","duration_ms":256853,"uuid":"393c0ce9-bc8c-4c8b-ac9c-4cfd2f3f3f19"}
